    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Public Tender - Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) Implementation of an AI assistance solution for hospital staff 1." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must let staff quickly access reliable, up-to-date information drawn from the authority's internal procedures, care protocols and HAS recommendations, applicable regulatory texts, and internal documents (guides, notes, reference frameworks, drug references)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk100> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By leveraging our company Faber IA expertise, experience, and partnerships, our company Faber IA can propose a comprehensive solution that addresses the client's requirements and constraints, while ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements and data protection regulations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk101> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires a solution that must be accessible from the hospital staff work environment, capable of supporting hospital staff in clinical administrative activities, fit into existing practices of staff, not introduce a rupture in clinical or administrative workflows, let staff access reliable up-to-date information, adapt generated content to the clinical administrative context, conform to expected quality standards, support medical coding for activity reporting (PMSI, ICD-10), take into account dossier context where available, provide response times compatible with daily clinical use, achieve response time below 2 seconds for common queries, ensure continuity of care with high level of availability including 24/7 services, have availability of the order of 99.9%, integrate with existing hospital information system (SIH), electronic patient record (DPI), health interoperability standards (HL7, FHIR), national health identifier (INS), and national framework (SGUR du numérique en santé, espace santé DMP)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk102> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must also be hosted on infrastructure that holds French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification, rely on low-carbon infrastructure, contribute to reducing energy consumption, and be conducted progressively." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk103> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "How do we design the technical architecture of The solution to meet these requirements?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk104> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To design the technical architecture of our proposed solution leverage we existing capabilities as described in the context. we Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform, Atelier, is a strong foundation for meeting many of the client's requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk105> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Firstly, to ensure accessibility and integration with the hospital staff work environment, we can utilize API-first design principles (REST + webhook) to embed The solution within existing workflows. utilize also satisfies the requirement for the solution to fit into existing practices without introducing disruptions." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk106> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For supporting hospital staff in clinical administrative activities and adapting generated content to the clinical administrative context, we components such as the document-ingestion pipeline, vector store, retrieval layer with hybrid search, orchestration layer, and answer layer will be crucial." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk107> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Atelier's components such as the document-ingestion pipeline, vector store, retrieval layer with hybrid search, orchestration layer, and answer layer can process and generate high-quality, context-specific content that conforms to expected quality standards." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk108> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding medical coding for activity reporting (PMSI, ICD-10), while we context does not explicitly mention support for expected quality standards, Our Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform, Atelier, model-agnostic nature means we can potentially integrate or support models trained on such data, assuming the availability of appropriate datasets and compliance with regulatory requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk109> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The requirement for response times compatible with daily clinical use, achieving response times below 2 seconds for common queries, and ensuring high availability (99.9%) aligns well with we performance metrics. we median latency is 1.3 seconds, and common single-document queries are below 2 seconds at p95. we achieve this through horizontal scaling with additional inference capacity." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must contextualise The solution answers to the staff member's request. 3.2 Drafting assistance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk110> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For integration with existing systems such as SIH, DPI, health interoperability standards (HL7, FHIR), and the national health identifier (INS), we architecture and integration capabilities include API design for embedding in work environments, health interoperability features like HL7 connectors, and support for identity management through SSO (SAML, OIDC) and user directories (LDAP, Entra ID)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk111> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To meet the hosting requirements, including French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification, reliance on low-carbon infrastructure, and contribution to reducing energy consumption, we can utilize we Sovereign HDS tier hosted on OuraneCloud. our Sovereign HDS tier hosted on OuraneCloud is SecNumCloud-qualified, HDS-certified, EU-only, and powered by renewable energy, aligning with the client's environmental and sovereignty constraints." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk112> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Lastly, conducting the project progressively, as required, involves phases that can be aligned with we capabilities for scalability and flexibility in deployment. we support on-premise/hybrid deployments where necessary, allowing for controlled rollout and testing within limited perimeters before generalizing to all services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk113> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In summary, by leveraging we robust architecture, integrating appropriate models for medical coding, utilizing we API-first approach for seamless integration, ensuring high performance and availability, and hosting the solution on a certified, environmentally friendly infrastructure, we can design a technical architecture that meets the client's comprehensive set of requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk114> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires that personal and health data must be protected, guaranteeing strict compliance with GDPR, processing health data as special category data under GDPR Art. 9, hosting data exclusively within the European Union, not transferring data outside the European Union, protecting sensitive data with encryption or pseudonymisation where relevant, providing explainable recommendations or suggestions, understanding elements that led to an output through source grounding and audit trail, using AI in healthcare consistently with guidance, not automating clinical or medico-administrative decisions without explicit validation by a qualified professional, and explicitly addressing implications of use case approaching medical device qualification CE marking MDR." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk115> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must also ensure data sovereignty, comply with regulatory requirements, provide a level of security, and integrate with existing SIH and DPI." ;
