    <http://example.org/node/chunk93> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Change-management support and staff training are expected. 10." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk94> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Evaluation criteria Offers will be evaluated against the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution; compliance with regulatory requirements; level of security; data sovereignty; quality of integration with the existing SIH/DPI; total cost of the proposed solution; consideration of environmental issues; capacity for innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk95> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires the implementation of an AI assistance solution for hospital staff, improvement of efficiency and quality of care delivered to patients, reduction of complexity of procedures, simplification of access to information sources, decrease of administrative and documentation work, increase of time available for patient care, facilitation of access to information, improvement of quality of written outputs, reduction of processing and documentation times, assistance in daily activities, provision of intelligent assistance tools, retrieval of information from internal procedures, care protocols, and applicable regulation, assistance in drafting medical and administrative documents, support in handling dossiers, continuity of care between professionals' shifts and services, fitting into existing practices, avoiding rupture in clinical or administrative processes, obtaining information consultation assistance, accessing reliable up-to-date information, applying authority's internal procedures, care protocols, and recommendations, complying with applicable regulatory texts, using internal documents, receiving contextualised answers to requests, obtaining drafting assistance, assisting in drafting of clinical and administrative content, drafting discharge summaries, medical reports, medical correspondence, patient letters, administrative documents, dossier syntheses, adapting generated content to the clinical administrative context, conforming to expected quality standards, providing dossier handling assistance, analysing and handling dossiers, surfacing relevant information, recalling applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications, supporting medical coding for activity reporting, taking into account dossier context, making non-automated decisions, protecting personal and health data, guaranteeing strict compliance with GDPR, processing health data as special category data under GDPR Art. 9, hosting data exclusively within the European Union, not transferring data outside the European Union, protecting sensitive data with encryption or pseudonymisation where relevant, holding French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification for infrastructure hosting the solution, providing explainable recommendations or suggestions, understanding elements that led to an output through source grounding and audit trail, using AI in healthcare consistently with guidance, not automating clinical or medico-administrative decisions without explicit validation by a qualified professional, not requiring medical device qualification CE marking MDR, explicitly addressing implications of use case approaching medical device qualification CE marking MDR, providing response times compatible with daily clinical use, achieving response time below 2 seconds for common queries, ensuring continuity of care with high level of availability including 24/7 services, having availability of the order of 99.9%, integrating with existing hospital information system (SIH), electronic patient record (DPI), health interoperability standards (HL7, FHIR), national health identifier (INS), national framework (SGUR du numérique en santé, espace santé DMP), considering environmental issues, and demonstrating capacity for innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk96> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given these requirements, how do we ensure that we proposed solution addresses all the necessary aspects and constraints?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk97> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address the client's requirements, our company Faber IA can leverage our company Faber IA flagship product Atelier, a sovereign platform that forges document-grounded AI assistants from an organisation's own documents. its flagship product Atelier, a sovereign platform that forges document-grounded AI assistants from an organisation's own documents can be tailored to provide intelligent assistance tools for hospital staff, improving efficiency and quality of care delivered to patients. our company Faber IA hybrid delivery model, combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure, is suited to public and health procurement. our company Faber IA will work closely with the client through joint steering and operational committees, ensuring that our proposed solution meets the client needs and complies with regulatory requirements. our company Faber IA can draw on our company Faber IA experience from past references, such as our company Faber IA work with a regional hospital group, where our company Faber IA implemented a pilot assistant for medical documentation integrated with a regional hospital group electronic patient record. our proposed solution will be designed to fit into existing practices, avoiding rupture in clinical or administrative processes, and ensuring continuity of care between professionals' shifts and services. its flagship product Atelier, a sovereign platform that forges document-grounded AI assistants from an organisation's own documents can provide contextualised answers to requests, assist in drafting medical and administrative documents, and support dossier handling. our company Faber IA will ensure that our proposed solution conforms to expected quality standards, adapts generated content to the clinical administrative context, and provides explainable recommendations or suggestions." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk98> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding data protection, our company Faber IA will guarantee strict compliance with GDPR, process health data as special category data under GDPR Art. 9, and host data exclusively within the European Union. our company Faber IA partner, OuraneCloud, is a French sovereign cloud provider (SecNumCloud-qualified, HDS-certified), which will be used as the hosting layer." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk99> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure integration with existing systems, our company Faber IA will work with our company Faber IA partner Ligeo Santé, a health-IT integrator, to integrate our proposed solution with the hospital's information system (SIH), electronic patient record (DPI), and health interoperability standards (HL7, FHIR). our company Faber IA will also consider environmental issues and demonstrate capacity for innovation. our proposed solution will be designed to provide response times compatible with daily clinical use, achieve response time below 2 seconds for common queries, and ensure continuity of care with a high level of availability, including 24/7 services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

